title: The Guomindang out of Funds
new-page: true
view-if: funds < 0

= The Guomindang out of Funds

We're in trouble. Because of our recent expenditures, we are now in debt. What should we do?

- @tax: Increase taxes.
- @print: Print more money.
- @cutnra: Take some funds out of the army.
- @bad: There's nothing we can do.

@tax
subtitle: +2 funds [? if centralize > 0 : (+1 for tax reforms) ?], +1 every quarter
unavailable-subtitle: Tax rates are already too high.
choose-if: upper_tax_rates <= 5 and lower_tax_rates <= 5
on-arrival: funds += 2; income += 1; funds += 1 if centralize > 0; new_middle_kmt -= 4; old_middle_kmt -= 4; workers_kmt -= 4; unemployed += 0.2; lower_tax_rates += 1; upper_tax_rates += 1; workers_kmt -= 5 if lower_tax_rates > 1; inflation -= 1.1; economic_growth -= 0.6; new_middle_kmt -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_kmt -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1;

People hate taxes, that's a given.

@print
subtitle: +2 funds - this will considerably level up inflation.
unavailable-subtitle: Inflation is getting too high.
choose-if: inflation < 10
on-arrival: funds += 2; inflation += 3; new_middle_kmt -= 4; old_middle_kmt -= 4; workers_kmt -= 4; unemployed += 2; workers_kmt -= 5 if lower_tax_rates > 1; inflation -= 1.1; economic_growth -= 0.6; new_middle_kmt -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1; old_middle_kmt -= 2 if upper_tax_rates > 1;

Issuing more sums of cash will start taking a toll on our inflation.
  
@cutnra
subtitle: +2 funds - the officers won't like this, and certainly not your men either.
unavailable-subtitle: The army is already barebones.
choose-if: nra_militancy > 0
on-arrival: funds += 2; nra_militancy -= 0.1; whampoa_dissent += 10;

The army has been defunded. What does this do for us?

@bad
subtitle: -1 quarterly income - we are forced to pay loan interest.
on-arrival: income -= 1;

Looks like our financial situation is getting dire. We now have to pay loan interests to keep our deficit managable.
